# Build context exclusions for `docker build`.
#
# The Dockerfile installs dependencies (`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`) and
# then runs `COPY . .`. Without this file that COPY overwrites the freshly
# installed `node_modules` and any prior `.next` output with whatever happened
# to be sitting in the build agent's workspace — so the image ships a stale
# build, compiled against a different environment. Everything here is either
# regenerated inside the image or has no business in it.

# Installed and built in the image itself (Dockerfile stage 1).
node_modules
.next
out
build
*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated by `msw init` (the `predev`/`pretest` hook). It is a service worker
# that intercepts fetches and serves mocks; shipping it to production would put
# a request interceptor on the deployed app. Not committed, but it exists in a
# developer's or agent's working tree.
public/mockServiceWorker.js

# Secrets. API_BASE_URL is passed as a --build-arg by the Jenkins pipelines;
# nothing in the image should be reading a local env file.
.env
.env.*
*.pem

# VCS and CI — not read at build or runtime. Excluding .git also keeps the
# context small, since it carries the whole history.
.git
.gitignore
Jenkinsfile
Jenkinsfile.main
ci
docker-compose.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
nginx.conf

# Docs and editor/agent state.
docs
.github
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude
.agents
.vscode
.idea

# Local noise.
coverage
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
